      },
      "text": "Electroacoustics is the conversion between acoustic (pressure/velocity) and electrical\n(voltage/current) energy. Microphones convert acoustic → electrical; loudspeakers do the reverse.\nAll transducers obey the same reciprocity principle."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md#003",
      "path": [
