        "root_concepts": "[electroacoustics]",
        "section": "acoustics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Electroacoustics - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PHYSICS: Faraday's law — coil moves in magnetic field → EMF = B·l·v\n         v = velocity of diaphragm (acoustic particle velocity)\n         Output voltage ∝ diaphragm velocity (velocity microphone)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:acoustics:06-electroacoustics, git-history:acoustics:06-electroacoustics]",
        "canonical_path": "acoustics/06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md",
        "concepts": "[electroacoustics]",
        "current_path": "acoustics/06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:acoustics:electroacoustics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "acoustics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[electroacoustics]",
        "section": "acoustics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Electroacoustics - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CHARACTERISTICS:\n• Robust, handles high SPL (130+ dB), doesn't need power\n• Limited low-frequency response (mass of coil + diaphragm)\n• Typically ±3 dB from 50 Hz – 15 kHz (decent dynamic range)\n• Self-noise: 14–20 dB SPL equivalent\n• Use: live vocals, drums, guitar amps (Shure SM58, SM57)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:acoustics:06-electroacoustics, git-history:acoustics:06-electroacoustics]",
        "canonical_path": "acoustics/06-ELECTROACOUSTICS.md",
