        "root_concepts": "[electroacoustics]",
        "section": "acoustics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Electroacoustics - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROXIMITY EFFECT:\nClose-miking (< 30 cm) of directional dynamics: bass frequencies boosted.\nCause: pressure gradient mics (cardioid) have a distance-dependent low-frequency response.\nF_bass boost = ∝ 1/distance at low frequencies.\n```"
    },
